---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Squiggle from '../components/Squiggle.astro';
import ConditionsGrid from '../components/ConditionsGrid.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="What Psychosexual Therapy Can Help With | Charnwood Intimacy"
  description="From low desire and painful sex to sexual trauma and intimacy problems, see how psychosexual therapy in Loughborough and online can help."
  path="/what-we-help-with/"
>
  <section class="section section--white intro-section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">What We Help With</p>
      <h1>What psychosexual therapy can help with</h1>
      <Squiggle />
      <p class="lead">
        Psychosexual therapy is a specialist form of talking therapy focused on sexual health,
        intimacy and the relational side of sexual experience. It draws on how our thoughts,
        feelings, history, relationships and physical experience all interact, and addresses
        difficulties in a holistic, compassionate and evidence-based way.
      </p>
      <p class="lead">
        It is not sex education, and it never involves any physical examination or contact.
        Sessions take place in exactly the same way as any other talking therapy: a private
        conversation, in a calm room or online, between you and your therapist. It's suitable
        for individuals and couples, of any gender, sexuality or relationship structure.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--blush">
    <div class="container topic-grid">
      <div class="topic">
        <h2>Sexual function</h2>
        <p>
          Difficulties with desire, arousal, orgasm or erection are common, and can affect anyone
          at any stage of life. See our dedicated pages on low desire and mismatched libido,
          painful sex and vaginismus, and erectile dysfunction and performance anxiety.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="topic">
        <h2>Sexual trauma and its effects</h2>
        <p>
          Past experiences of sexual abuse, assault or coercion can shape how we feel about sex,
          intimacy and our own bodies long afterwards. See our dedicated page on sexual trauma.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="topic">
        <h2>Intimacy and relationships</h2>
        <p>
          Sexual difficulties rarely exist in isolation from a relationship. See our dedicated
          page on couples and intimacy therapy, covering mismatched libido, loss of connection,
          and rebuilding intimacy after infidelity, illness or a major life change.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="topic">
        <h2>Identity, behaviour and self-worth</h2>
        <p>
          Our sense of ourselves as sexual beings is closely tied to confidence, identity and
          self-worth. See our dedicated page on compulsive sexual behaviour and porn use, and
          speak to us about any other concern relating to sexual identity, shame or
          self-consciousness that isn't listed here. If it's affecting you, it's worth talking
          about.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--white">
    <div class="container">
      <h2>Explore each area</h2>
      <ConditionsGrid />
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .intro-section .lead {
    max-width: 780px;
    font-size: 1.1rem;
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  .topic-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;
    gap: 32px;
  }
  .topic p {
    color: var(--text-soft);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .topic-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
    }
  }
</style>
